          <h1 class="top-two triple-extra-large-text bold-scripted tight-track deepest-gray-text sm-quad-extra-large-text">Copper Compass Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="top-eight">Copper Compass Privacy Policy</p>
          <p class="top-eight">Copper Compass respects your privacy. This policy explains how we collect, use, store, and share personal information when you play our games or use related services. It applies to players in England and is intended to reflect applicable UK data protection laws, including the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.</p>
          <p class="top-eight">
            Information we may collect Depending on the game and features you use, we may collect: • Information you provide, such as a username, profile details, or messages sent to support. • Game and device information, such as your game progress, settings, device type, operating system, language, and app version. • Usage and diagnostic data, such as feature interactions, session information, crash reports, and performance data. • Purchase information. Payments are generally processed by the
            relevant platform or payment provider; we may receive transaction details needed to provide purchases and support. • Information provided by third-party services you choose to use, such as platform sign-in services.
          </p>
          <p class="top-eight">How we use information We use information to operate and improve our games, save progress, provide features and support, process or verify purchases, maintain security, prevent fraud or misuse, understand performance, and meet legal obligations. Where required, we rely on an appropriate legal basis, such as providing the service you request, our legitimate interests, your consent, or compliance with a legal obligation.</p>
          <p class="top-eight">
            Sharing information We may share limited information with service providers that help us operate, host, analyze, or support our games, and with platform or payment providers when needed. These providers may process information only for the services they provide to us and subject to appropriate safeguards. We may also disclose information where required by law or necessary to protect the rights, safety, and security of players, Copper Compass, or others. We do not sell personal
            information.
          </p>
          <p class="top-eight">International transfers Some service providers may process information outside the United Kingdom. Where this happens, we use legally required safeguards for international transfers.</p>
          <p class="top-eight">Retention and security We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including providing the game, resolving disputes, and meeting legal requirements. We use appropriate technical and organizational measures to help protect information, but no method of storage or transmission is completely secure.</p>
          <p class="top-eight">
            Your rights Depending on the circumstances, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the use of your personal information, object to certain processing, request a copy of your information, or withdraw consent where processing is based on consent. You may also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO). To exercise your rights, contact Copper Compass using the support or contact details provided in the game or its store listing.
          </p>
          <p class="top-eight">Children Our games are not intended to collect personal information from children where doing so would be unlawful. If you believe a child has provided personal information without appropriate authorization, contact us using the support or contact details provided in the game or its store listing so we can review and take appropriate action.</p>
          <p class="top-eight">Third-party services Our games may include links to or integrations with third-party services. Those services have their own privacy policies, and Copper Compass is not responsible for their privacy practices. Please review their policies before using them.</p>
          <p class="top-eight">Changes to this policy We may update this policy from time to time. We will publish the current version with the game or on its relevant store page. Any changes take effect when the updated policy is published.</p>
          <p class="top-eight">Contact For questions or requests about this policy or your personal information, contact Copper Compass through the support or contact details provided in the game or its store listing.</p>
